# i18n: zero em dashes in labels

Never use the em dash (`—`, U+2014) or en dash (`–`, U+2013) as punctuation in **user-facing** strings (buttons, titles, body copy, hints, aria-labels, tooltips, empty states, tour text, settings).

## Forbidden

| Hack | Why |
|---|---|
| `Here we’ll place Mirador for you — click “…”.` | AI-default clause dash; reads fake |
| `Help — replay the introduction` | Same |
| `Loading — {label}` | Same |
| En dash as a clause separator (`text – more`) | Same family; do not use |

## Do instead

- Split into two sentences: `…. ….`
- Use a colon for label/value: `Loading: {label}`
- Use the middle dot already in the product: `A · B`
- Use a hyphen only inside real compound words (`right-click`, `near-field`), never as a clause break

## Scope

- Applies to `src/i18n/locales/**` and any hardcoded user-visible string (which should already live in i18n).
- Does **not** apply to code comments, license legalese credits, or numeric ranges written with ASCII hyphen-minus (`0.2-0.4`).

## Rule of landing

A UI string that contains `—` or a clause-breaking `–` is a failed change. Rewrite before merge.
